mainline_probe_stdlib_feature_modules: 2026-07-31 continued the mainline Swift route by staging the official Swift 6.0.3 string-processing source repository swiftlang/swift-experimental-string-processing tag swift-6.0.3-RELEASE commit 9c50f6da9be4b4a828cec31adbef758a6c3673d6. The transferred archive was verified with sha256 19b615d31d904326bbb73fed9510524c66db3a00a7b133bc0fa2f681b48023b4 and unpacked on the true device at /storage/Users/currentUser/swift-mainline-ohos-src/deps/swift-experimental-string-processing-src. The existing OHOS Swift build tree was reconfigured with SWIFT_ENABLE_EXPERIMENTAL_CONCURRENCY=ON, SWIFT_CONCURRENCY_GLOBAL_EXECUTOR=hooked, SWIFT_ENABLE_EXPERIMENTAL_STRING_PROCESSING=ON, and SWIFT_PATH_TO_STRING_PROCESSING_SOURCE pointing to that staged source. reconfigure-swift-stdlib-concurrency-stringprocessing-20260731-161744.log completed with CMAKE_RC=0 and generated OHOS targets for _Concurrency, _RegexParser, _StringProcessing, and RegexBuilder. The first guarded build nice -n 10 ninja -j1 swift_Concurrency-ohos in build-swift-Concurrency-ohos-j1-20260731-161949.log rebuilt affected Swift compiler C++ libraries, linked a new bin/swift-frontend at [910/1041], and then failed at [913/1041] while compiling stdlib/public/core/OHOS/aarch64/Swift.o. The failing pass was AArch64 Assembly Printer and the command ended with Segmentation fault / signal 11 / NINJA_RC=1. This is the same direct object-emission class previously handled through IR-to-OHOS-clang handoff, not a new source-level _Concurrency or Regex failure. Next step is to regenerate Swift.o through the proven IR handoff under SWIFT_ENABLE_EXPERIMENTAL_CONCURRENCY=ON and SWIFT_ENABLE_EXPERIMENTAL_STRING_PROCESSING=ON, then resume swift_Concurrency-ohos before attempting _RegexParser, _StringProcessing, RegexBuilder, FoundationEssentials, SwiftPM, or unxip CI. Post-failure monitoring at 2026-07-31 18:40:24 CST showed no residual Swift/ninja process, MemAvailable 14524416 kB, and SwapFree 49467636 kB.
mainline_probe_foundationessentials: 2026-08-01 advanced the OHOS-native Swift path through FoundationEssentials. The full primary-file IR handoff in probe-foundationessentials-primary-handoff-20260801-005338.log reused the module and completed clang_ok=182/182 with status=0 and no real errors. Output-file-map audit found filemap_records=182, objects_present=182, nonzero=182, missing=0, zero=0, objects_total_size=17241976, and FoundationEssentials.swiftmodule size=3987972. Direct ninja was avoided because the original Swift WMO edge remained dirty due missing .ninja_log command history. Manual link sequencing ran the audit, _FoundationCShims C compiles, lib_FoundationCShims.a, and lib_FoundationCollections.a while skipping only the original swiftc -c -emit-module -wmo command. The first link failed on duplicate BigString conformance symbols from lib_FoundationCollections.a; llvm-nm found duplicate_symbols=176 among defined_symbols=5573. A bootstrap retry adding -Xlinker --allow-multiple-definition linked lib/libFoundationEssentials.so with size=13426176. llvm-readobj showed an aarch64 ELF shared object needing libswiftSwiftOnoneSupport.so, libswiftCore.so, libswift_Concurrency.so, libswift_StringProcessing.so, libswiftGlibc.so, and libc.so, with a malformed RUNPATH ending in :::::::: . A minimal true-device executable importing FoundationEssentials compiled and ran with compile_rc=0 and run_rc=0 in probe-foundationessentials-exe-20260801-022741.log, printing 0. Remaining work is to replace the muldefs bootstrap with correct weak/linkonce handling for IR-handoff archives, clean RUNPATH, formalize or remove OHOS_BOOTSTRAP_NO_MACROS, and make the handoff/link path repeatable before SwiftPM or unxip validation.
mainline_probe_foundationessentials_weaken_archive: 2026-08-01 follow-up reduced the FoundationEssentials duplicate-symbol boundary from final-link muldefs to targeted archive symbol weakening. llvm-nm showed only two strong duplicate symbols in lib_FoundationCollections.a: $s22_FoundationCollections9BigStringVSlAAMc with R,R and $s22_FoundationCollections9BigStringVSlAAWP with D,D. A copy of the archive was processed with llvm-objcopy --weaken-symbol for those two symbols; llvm-nm then reported V weak entries. Linking FoundationEssentials against lib_FoundationCollections.weakened.a succeeded without --allow-multiple-definition in run-foundationessentials-link-weaken-fc-validname-20260801-023624.log with link_rc=0 and size=13426176. The build-tree standard artifact names were switched to the weakened archive and weakened-link so, with backups lib_FoundationCollections.pre-weaken-20260801-023756.a, libFoundationEssentials.muldefs-20260801-023756.so, and libFoundationEssentials.muldefs-active-20260801-023917.so. The standard lib/libFoundationEssentials.so path was revalidated by probe-foundationessentials-standard-exe-20260801-023951.log with compile_rc=0, run_rc=0, and stdout 0. Remaining mainline work is to make duplicate strong-symbol detection/weakening part of the repeatable IR-handoff archive rule.
mainline_probe_foundationessentials_clean_rpath: 2026-08-01 traced the malformed FoundationEssentials RUNPATH ending in :::::::: to the explicit empty CMake rpath fragment -Xlinker -rpath -Xlinker ::::::: in the final link command. Relinking without that fragment, while using the weakened _FoundationCollections archive, succeeded in run-foundationessentials-link-clean-rpath-20260801-024228.log with link_rc=0. llvm-readobj then reported RUNPATH=/storage/Users/currentUser/swift-mainline-ohos-src/build/swift-manual-ohos-linuxsys2/lib/swift/ohos and the same expected NEEDED set. The clean-rpath shared object passed probe-foundationessentials-clean-rpath-exe-20260801-024307.log with compile_rc=0, run_rc=0, and stdout 0. The standard build-tree lib/libFoundationEssentials.so now points to the clean-rpath, weakened-archive-linked artifact; the prior weak but dirty-rpath file was backed up as libFoundationEssentials.weak-rpathdirty-20260801-024335.so.
mainline_probe_foundationcollections_archive_helper: 2026-08-01 updated the true-device tmp/archive_foundationcollections.py helper so archive generation automatically detects strong duplicate symbols with llvm-nm and weakens them with llvm-objcopy. Regression log archive-foundationcollections-irhandoff-20260801-024636.log reported OBJECTS=155, BAD=0, AR_RC=0, DEFINED_SYMBOLS=5825, STRONG_DUPLICATES=2, WEAKEN_RC=0, post-weaken STRONG_DUPLICATES=0, FINAL_OUT_SIZE=4267186, END_RC=0. This makes the duplicate-symbol fix repeatable at archive-helper level.
mainline_probe_foundationessentials_link_helper: 2026-08-01 added true-device tmp/link_foundationessentials_from_handoff.py to capture the FoundationEssentials handoff-to-link sequence. The helper reads ninja -t commands lib/libFoundationEssentials.so, skips only the original swiftc -c -emit-module -wmo command, runs the audit step, _FoundationCShims commands, the updated archive_foundationcollections.py helper, removes the empty rpath fragment from the final link command, links a clean shared object, and installs lib/libFoundationEssentials.so. Regression log link-foundationessentials-from-handoff-20260801-024854.log reported COMMANDS=9, SKIP_ORIGINAL_WMO=1, RC=0, clean RUNPATH to the Swift OHOS runtime directory, and the expected NEEDED set. probe-foundationessentials-after-helper-exe-20260801-024935.log then compiled and ran a minimal FoundationEssentials executable with compile_rc=0, run_rc=0, stdout 0.
mainline_probe_foundationessentials_ninja_integrated: 2026-08-01 integrated the FoundationEssentials handoff result back into the generated Foundation Ninja build tree. The remote build tree was backed up as CMakeFiles/rules.ninja.pre-fe-noop-20260801-030146.bak and build.ninja.pre-fe-noop-20260801-030146.bak, then only the FoundationEssentials WMO compile edge was made a no-op and only its final LINK_LIBRARIES empty-rpath fragment was removed. The guarded nice -n 10 ninja -j1 FoundationEssentials run in ninja-foundationessentials-integrated-20260801-030348.log completed with BUILD_RC=0; ninja -n FoundationEssentials then reported no work to do. llvm-readobj on lib/libFoundationEssentials.so reported a clean RUNPATH to /storage/Users/currentUser/swift-mainline-ohos-src/build/swift-manual-ohos-linuxsys2/lib/swift/ohos and NEEDED libraries libswiftSwiftOnoneSupport.so, libswiftCore.so, libswift_Concurrency.so, libswift_StringProcessing.so, libswiftGlibc.so, and libc.so. A fresh executable probe in probe-foundationessentials-after-ninja-exe-20260801-030631.log returned compile_rc=0 and run_rc=0. The run used TMPDIR=/storage/Users/currentUser/swift-mainline-ohos-src/tmp after a read-only default temp failure, single-job Ninja, nice priority, and monitor-foundationessentials-integrated-20260801-030348.log, which showed about 13.26 GiB MemAvailable and 48.93 GiB SwapFree at start.
mainline_probe_foundationinternationalization: 2026-08-01 advanced FoundationInternationalization after FoundationEssentials Ninja integration. Direct WMO object emission in build-foundationinternationalization-j1-20260801-031425.log failed with Swift frontend signal 11 while the device remained memory-safe, matching the existing OHOS/aarch64 direct object-emission crash class. A target-specific primary-file IR handoff helper tmp/probe_foundationinternationalization_primary_handoff.py completed 60/60 primary files and 60 object files with rc=0 in probe-foundationinternationalization-primary-handoff-20260801-032408.log, ending with about 12.76 GiB MemAvailable. The generated Foundation Ninja tree was backed up as CMakeFiles/rules.ninja.pre-fi-noop-20260801-035103.bak and build.ninja.pre-fi-noop-20260801-035103.bak, then patched only around the FoundationInternationalization WMO edge and link variables. ninja-foundationinternationalization-integrated-20260801-035129.log completed with BUILD_RC=0, and ninja -n FoundationInternationalization reported no work to do. The resulting libFoundationInternationalization.so has RUNPATH to the Swift OHOS runtime and Foundation lib dir and NEEDED entries for libFoundationEssentials.so, lib_FoundationICU.so, Swift runtimes, and libc.so. A minimal import FoundationInternationalization executable now compiles, but probe-foundationinternationalization-exe-20260801-035444.log fails at runtime with run_rc=127 due loader errors for lib_FoundationICU.so and unresolved ICU symbols. Sampled ICU symbols are exported from lib_FoundationICU.so, so the next boundary is loader policy or dynamic metadata: lib_FoundationICU.so has RUNPATH :::::::, NEEDED libc++_shared.so and libc.so, and no observed .codesign section, while libFoundationInternationalization.so has .codesign. Next probes should verify signing, dirty RUNPATH cleanup, and libc++_shared.so resolution before broader Foundation, SwiftPM, or unxip validation.
mainline_probe_foundation_full: 2026-08-01 resumed the Foundation main module after SSH recovery and safe memory checks. The previous import Foundation smoke runtime failed because libFoundation.so referenced posix_spawn_file_actions_addchdir, which the tested OHOS libc does not export. Generated C flags define __OHOS__ and __MUSL__, while upstream CFPlatform.c only checked lower-case __musl__, so OHOS fell through to the POSIX.1-2024 addchdir call. A probe patch in swift-corelibs-foundation/Sources/CoreFoundation/CFPlatform.c now returns ENOSYS for _CFPosixSpawnFileActionsChdir when defined(__OHOS__). nice -n 10 ninja -j4 Foundation completed with RC=0 in build-Foundation-after-ohos-addchdir-j4-20260801-1215.log, rebuilding CFPlatform.c.o, libCoreFoundation.a, libFoundationInternationalization.so, and libFoundation.so. Runtime shared libraries were re-signed in sign-foundation-runtime-after-ohos-addchdir-20260801-1218.log with RC=0. A fresh minimal executable importing Foundation compiled and ran on the true device: foundation-smoke-compile-20260801-121709.log COMPILE_RC=0, run-foundation-smoke-after-ohos-addchdir-20260801-1218.console.log RUN_RC=0, stdout foundation-smoke 0. Monitoring remained safe with about 14 GiB MemAvailable and 49 GiB SwapFree at smoke start. Remaining mainline work is to formalize the temporary OHOS CoreFoundation patch, IR handoff/no-op Ninja integrations, runtime signing, and SwiftPM/new-driver path before returning to unxip validation.
mainline_probe_swift_new_driver: 2026-08-01 true-device new-driver prototype completed IR handoff for SwiftDriver (110/110 primary files, link_rc=0, libSwiftDriver.so 7929216 bytes), SwiftDriverExecution (3/3 primary files, link_rc=0, libSwiftDriverExecution.so 339328 bytes), and the final swift-driver executable (emit_ir_rc=0, objectize_rc=0, link_rc=0, exe_size=89600) in probe-swiftdriver-handoff-20260801-151610.log, probe-swiftdriverexecution-handoff-20260801-161556.log, and probe-swift-driver-exe-handoff-20260801-164004.log. SwiftScan/Loader.swift now guards RTLD_DEEPBIND with !OHOS. libllbuildSwift.so needs terminfo symbols setupterm/tigetnum/set_curterm/del_curterm, satisfied by /storage/Users/currentUser/usr/local/lib/libtinfo.so.6 with RUNPATH updated by the executable handoff. Runtime validation works when invoked through copied argv0 names because symlinks are denied: with TMPDIR set to the Swift probe tmp and PATH including build/swift-manual-ohos-linuxsys2/bin, build/swift-driver-ohos-probe5/probe-bin/swiftc -version reports Swift version 6.0.3 target aarch64-unknown-linux-ohos and -print-target-info reports target.triple aarch64-unknown-linux-ohos. Remaining boundaries are formalizing the IR handoff/Ninja rule changes, removing probe logging, deciding the argv0 install strategy, staging swift-help, and building SwiftPM subcommands before returning to unxip validation.

mainline_probe_swift_new_driver_linkerfix: 2026-08-01 follow-up rebuilt the Swift new-driver probe after a narrow OHOS linker-selection experiment in SwiftDriver/Jobs/GenericUnixToolchain+LinkerSupport.swift. The patch selects /storage/Users/currentUser/usr/local/bin/clang-15 instead of the non-executable clang shell wrapper for OHOS targets, injects /storage/Users/currentUser/usr/local/sysroot when no SDK is supplied, defaults OHOS links to lld, and adds -Wl,--code-sign. Rebuild logs probe-swiftdriver-handoff-20260801-181706.log, probe-swiftdriverexecution-handoff-20260801-191242.log, and probe-swift-driver-exe-handoff-20260801-191435.log all ended rc=0. A fresh copied argv0 probe directory /storage/Users/currentUser/swift-mainline-ohos-src/tmp/probe-bin-linkerpatch2-20260801-1916 was used because the old probe-bin files were not writable by the SSH user. With SWIFT_DRIVER_CLANG_EXEC unset and no explicit -sdk or -use-ld on the hello compile, swiftc -version, -print-target-info, and -help returned rc=0; -### showed clang-15, -fuse-ld=lld, --sysroot /storage/Users/currentUser/usr/local/sysroot, and -Wl,--code-sign; the produced hello executable printed hello-new-driver-ohos with run_rc=0. Current next boundary is SwiftPM command availability (swift-package/swift-build), not single-file new-driver linking.
mainline_probe_swiftpm_deps_pemfix: 2026-08-01 SwiftPM configure advanced into package dependency configs and exposed missing SwiftASN1, SwiftCrypto, and SwiftCertificates CMake packages. Manual OHOS-native probes produced SwiftASN1, SwiftCrypto Crypto, SwiftCrypto _CryptoExtras, and swift-certificates _CertificateInternals artifacts through the established primary-file IR handoff. The first X509 probe failed during emit-module because PEMDocument, PEMRepresentable, PEMParseable, and PEMSerializable were absent from the rebuilt SwiftASN1 module. Upstream SwiftASN1 gates PEMDocument.swift behind canImport(Foundation) || canImport(FoundationEssentials); rebuilding SwiftASN1 with build/foundation-ohos-probe1/swift, libdispatch Swift module paths, and Foundation client C modulemaps made PEMDocument.swift emit/objectize successfully and linked libSwiftASN1.so with link_rc=0 in probe-swiftasn1-handoff-20260801-2143-foundation.log. asn1-pem-smoke-20260801-215352.log typechecked PEMDocument, PEMRepresentable, PEMSerializable, and PEMParseable with rc=0. The follow-up X509 probe probe-cert-X509-handoff-20260801-2155-pemfix.log passed emit_module_rc=0 for 99 sources and continued object emission under single-frontend nice -n 10 monitoring with about 13 GiB MemAvailable. Remaining boundary before unxip package validation is completing X509/libX509.so, staging SwiftCertificatesConfig.cmake, and getting runnable SwiftPM entry points swift-package/swift-build.
mainline_probe_swiftpm_entrypoints: 2026-08-02 OHOS-native SwiftPM entry points now run a minimal package under diagnostic supports. build/swiftpm-ohos-probe1/bin/swift-package and swift-build both report Swift Package Manager - Swift 6.0.3. PackageDescription.swiftmodule, swiftdoc, swiftsourceinfo, and libPackageDescription.so were copied beside the SwiftPM executables so direct $SPM/bin dump-package works without the temporary swiftpm-bin-manifestapi-copy shim. libllbuildSwift.so was relinked with -l:libtinfo.so.6 in relink-llbuildswift-tinfo-linkonly-20260802-112804.log; llvm-objdump -p now reports NEEDED libtinfo.so.6 and swift-build --version runs without LD_PRELOAD=libtinfo.so.6. Minimal package smokes passed in swift-build-smoke-no-tinfo-preload-20260802-112915 and swift-build-smoke-spmbin-20260802-113522, each producing Build complete and a HelloOHOS executable that prints Hello, world! with rc=0. Remaining boundaries are the diagnostic libdispatch/concurrency hook, diagnostic swiftc modulewrap shim, manual SDK/resource-dir/Glibc modulemap flags, SwiftCrypto diagnostic AES-GCM workaround, OHOS symlink warning, and cleanup/formalization of probe logging and IR handoff scripts before unxip validation.
mainline_probe_swiftpm_dispatch_sdk: 2026-08-02 follow-up rebuilt libswift_Concurrency.so with SWIFT_CONCURRENCY_USES_DISPATCH=1, staged OHOS libdispatch link paths, and an IR-to-llc handoff for _Concurrency.o after direct Swift backend codegen continued to crash on the AArch64/OHOS debug-info path. build-concurrency-dispatch-pic-uses-ninja-20260802-124248.log ended NINJA_RC=0; the resulting runtime exports swift_task_enqueueOnDispatchQueue, contains DispatchQueueShim witness-table symbols, and needs libdispatch.so plus libBlocksRuntime.so. A no-preload SwiftPM smoke then passed the old dispatch/runtime blocker and exposed missing manifest -sdk propagation instead of a missing sysroot. A signed native ELF swiftc wrapper at tmp/swiftc-modulewrap-sdkelf-20260802-1312 proved the narrow SDK/resource-dir/Glibc-modulemap fix: swiftpm-dump-sdkelf-20260802-1318.log returned RC=0. With --disable-index-store, swiftpm-build-sdkelf-noindex-20260802-1328.log built a debug package, swiftpm-run-audit-sdkelf-20260802-1333.log ran it and printed hello swiftpm ohos, and swiftpm-async-build-run-sdkelf-20260802-1400.log built and ran an async main plus Task.yield smoke printing async swiftpm ohos. Remaining boundaries are source/CMake formalization of dispatch and IR handoff, replacing the SDK ELF wrapper with real SwiftPM/toolchain sysroot propagation, fixing or disabling index-store for OHOS, replacing the modulewrap diagnostic shim, and investigating the release/-O Swift frontend crash.
mainline_probe_swiftpm_indexstore_fix: 2026-08-02 narrowed the SwiftPM default-index-store failure to ClangImporter driver argument propagation. The previous failing target compile passed -index-store-path to the OHOS clang driver, causing unknown argument and expected exactly one compiler job errors. An experimental patch in repos/swift/lib/ClangImporter/ClangImporter.cpp filters IndexStorePath from clang driver arguments when the target triple string contains ohos; rebuild log rebuild-swiftfrontend-indexstore-20260802-133739.log completed RC=0 and updated bin/swift-frontend/bin/swiftc. With explicit OHOS SDK/resource-dir/Glibc modulemap -Xswiftc flags and no --disable-index-store, swiftpm-indexstore-xswiftc-20260802-135449.log built and ran a debug package with RC=0 and stdout index store xswiftc ohos. swiftpm-async-indexstore-xswiftc-20260802-140136.log then built and ran async main with RC=0 and stdout async index store xswiftc ohos. During the probe, libswiftDispatch.so, libdispatch.so, and libBlocksRuntime.so had to be copied from build/libdispatch-ohos-swift-probe-linuxsys into build/swift-manual-ohos-linuxsys2/lib/swift/ohos because manifest execution resolves through RUNPATH rather than the outer LD_LIBRARY_PATH. Pure swift-build --triple still fails the final package link without manual SDK propagation, as shown by swiftpm-indexstore-default-stageddispatch-20260802-134907.log with missing Scrt1.o, crti.o, libc, and crtn.o, so the remaining boundary is proper SwiftPM/toolchain SDK propagation plus modulewrap/release formalization, not index-store.
mainline_probe_swiftpm_release_irhandoff: 2026-08-02 release SwiftPM was split into frontend and link stages. release-frontend-variants-20260802-141443.log shows -O -emit-sil passes, -O -emit-ir returns signal 5/RC 133 while writing non-empty IR, and direct -O object emission returns signal 11/RC 139 with a zero-byte object. release-irhandoff-link-20260802-141640.log proves the non-empty release IR can be objectized by the OHOS LLVM fork clang-15, linked with the staged Swift runtime and OHOS sysroot, signed, and run on the true device with stdout release xswiftc ohos and RUN_RC=0. Release mode is therefore feasible through IR handoff, but direct object emission and swiftc -modulewrap remain reviewable toolchain integration boundaries.
mainline_probe_swiftpm_default_sdk: 2026-08-02 rebuilt the SwiftDriver default SDK experiment for linux-ohos in build-swift-driver-defaultsdk-j1-20260802-1506.log with NINJA_RC=0 and link_rc=0. Driver.swift now asks the toolchain for defaultSDKPath and GenericUnixToolchain.defaultSDKPath reads OHOS_SDKROOT, OHOS_SYSROOT, or SDKROOT. With a full SwiftPM/SwiftDriver dependency LD_LIBRARY_PATH and OHOS_SDKROOT=/storage/Users/currentUser/usr/local/sysroot, fresh SwiftPM debug packages built through $MAN/bin/swift build without manual -Xswiftc -sdk flags. swiftpm-default-defaultsdk-swiftbuild-20260802-164449.log completed Build complete in 84.22s, RUN_RC=0, stdout default sdk swift build ohos. swiftpm-glibc-defaultsdk-swiftbuild-20260802-165044.log completed Build complete in 112.40s, RUN_RC=0, stdout glibc default sdk pid 46298. Logs show Swift frontend -sdk /storage/Users/currentUser/usr/local/sysroot, ClangImporter/link --sysroot /storage/Users/currentUser/usr/local/sysroot, and the Glibc smoke executable NEEDED libswiftGlibc.so plus libc.so. Final health at 2026-08-02 16:58 CST showed no residual heavy build process, MemAvailable about 14.9 GiB, and SwapFree about 49.2 GiB. Remaining boundary before unxip validation is formalizing SwiftDriver/SwiftPM patches, dispatch runtime staging, modulewrap behavior, and release IR handoff.
mainline_probe_swiftpm_release_sdkfix: 2026-08-02 evening true-device release probe validated a full SwiftPM release package importing Glibc through experimental signed IR handoff wrapper /storage/Users/currentUser/swift-mainline-ohos-src/tmp/swift-irhandoff-wrapper-sdkfix-20260802-190734. swiftpm-release-irhandoff-sdkfix-20260802-191210.log completed Build complete in 112.19s with BUILD_RC=0, RUN_RC=0, and stdout "swiftpm release sdkfix pid 23011". The wrapper intercepts optimized frontend -c, emits non-empty IR, accepts current frontend signal 5/RC 133 after IR write, strips debug metadata with opt, objectizes via OHOS clang-15 --sysroot /storage/Users/currentUser/usr/local/sysroot -fPIC -c, injects missing SDK/resource/Glibc modulemap search paths, and preserves signed OHOS final linking. The resulting executable uses /lib/ld-musl-aarch64.so.1, RUNPATH /storage/Users/currentUser/swift-mainline-ohos-src/build/swift-manual-ohos-linuxsys2/lib/swift/ohos:$ORIGIN, and NEEDED libswiftSwiftOnoneSupport.so, libswiftCore.so, libswift_Concurrency.so, libswift_StringProcessing.so, libswiftGlibc.so, libc.so. Remaining boundary is formalizing the IR handoff/modulewrap/SDK/code-signing behavior into reviewable Swift frontend-driver-build-system changes before unxip validation.
mainline_probe_swiftpm_release_concurrency: 2026-08-02 direct optimized object probes narrowed but did not replace IR handoff. probe-release-direct-debugmeta-20260802-192948.log showed debug and gnone variants returning RC=133 while writing non-empty ELF relocatable objects; probe-release-direct-debugmeta-link-20260802-192948.log proved both objects autolinked, linked, and ran with RUN_RC=0. However swiftpm-release-validobj-sdkfix-j2-20260802-193829.log showed a full SwiftPM release package using a valid-object wrapper still failed with BUILD_RC=1, RUN_RC=127, and frontend rc=139 valid_elf=0, so ignoring non-zero exits is not a general solution. The proven IR handoff wrapper then passed full SwiftPM release Glibc smoke with package concurrency -j2 and explicit frontend thread cap -Xswiftc -num-threads -Xswiftc 2 in swiftpm-release-irhandoff-sdkfix-j2-t2-20260802-194542.log: Build complete 112.51s, BUILD_RC=0, RUN_RC=0, stdout "swiftpm release irhandoff j2 t2 pid 12531". Monitoring stayed safe around 14 GiB MemAvailable and 49 GiB SwapFree. Future parallel probes should pair package-level -j with explicit Swift frontend thread caps.
mainline_probe_swiftpm_release_multitarget_j3: 2026-08-02 controlled concurrency was raised to SwiftPM -j3 with a three-library-target plus one executable-target release package, still using the signed IR handoff wrapper and explicit frontend thread cap request -Xswiftc -num-threads -Xswiftc 3. swiftpm-release-irhandoff-multitarget-j3-t3-20260802-195322.log completed Build complete in 166.72s with BUILD_RC=0, RUN_RC=0, and stdout "swiftpm release multitarget j3 t3 138". The executable used the OHOS musl loader, RUNPATH to the staged Swift OHOS runtime plus $ORIGIN, and expected NEEDED Swift runtime libraries plus libc.so. monitor-swiftpm-release-irhandoff-multitarget-j3-t3-20260802-195322.log stayed safe with lowest sampled MemAvailable about 13.7 GiB and SwapFree around 49.5 GiB. Diagnostic output still shows a layering issue where outer SwiftDriver commands may print -num-threads 20 while intercepted frontend commands include -num-threads 3, so thread control needs source-level formalization before higher concurrency becomes a default.
mainline_probe_swift_frontdoor_release: 2026-08-02 standard $MAN/bin/swift build front door was validated for the same three-library-target plus executable release package. The first attempt swift-man-build-release-multitarget-j3-t3-20260802-200331.log failed immediately with "error: unable to invoke subcommand: swift-build (No such file or directory)", showing the current layout still needs SwiftPM subcommands exposed beside swift or via PATH. After adding $SPM/bin to PATH, swift-man-build-release-multitarget-pathfix-j3-t3-20260802-200448.log completed Build complete in 167.69s with BUILD_RC=0, RUN_RC=0, and stdout "swift frontdoor pathfix release j3 t3 85". The executable used /lib/ld-musl-aarch64.so.1, RUNPATH to the staged Swift OHOS runtime plus $ORIGIN, and expected Swift runtime NEEDED entries plus libc.so. Remaining packaging boundary is installing/exposing SwiftPM subcommands and staging dependency libraries without oversized manual LD_LIBRARY_PATH.
mainline_probe_unxip_foundationxml_lzma: 2026-08-02 unxip/3.3 was retried as the first real SwiftPM package after release IR handoff and front-door swift build passed for synthetic packages. The source archive was staged at /storage/Users/currentUser/swift-mainline-ohos-src/tmp/unxip-v3.3.tar.gz and extracted to tmp/unxip-3.3-src; the upstream Sources/libunxip/libunxip.swift symlink had to be materialized as a normal file because the tested OHOS extraction path rejects that link. unxip-swiftpm-release-product-j3-t3-20260802-202917.log reached Swift compilation but failed on no such module Foundation. Adding build/foundation-ohos-probe1/swift moved the boundary forward. probe-unxip-import-matrix-20260802-205729.log showed IMPORT_GNUSource=0, IMPORT_getopt=0, IMPORT_zlib=0, IMPORT_Foundation=1, IMPORT_lzma=1, and IMPORT_FoundationXML=1. A direct Foundation client-modulemap smoke in probe-foundation-cmodule-paths-20260802-210746.log compiled and ran with RC_COMPILE=0 and RC_RUN=0 when the Foundation swift directory plus _foundation_unicode, _FoundationCShims, and CoreFoundation module maps were supplied. lzma is a separate xz/liblzma header boundary, confirmed by fatal error lzma.h file not found. FoundationXML is a Foundation staging boundary because foundation-ohos-probe1 was configured with FOUNDATION_ENABLE_XML=OFF. configure-foundation-xml-probe1-20260802-211222.log showed XML ON fails without LIBXML2_INCLUDE_DIR. The existing Conan cache package libxml2/2.15.3 at /storage/Users/currentUser/.conan2/p/libxma6fa3de616723/p supplies include/libxml2/libxml/xmlversion.h and lib/libxml2.so; configure-foundation-xml-probe2-20260802-212033.log then found LibXml2 version 2.15.3 and completed CONFIG_RC=0, generating _CFXMLInterface and FoundationXML targets. A fresh XML build directory would rebuild 574 Foundation/ICU steps, so the next efficient path is to seed/reuse validated foundation-ohos-probe1 artifacts and only compile _CFXMLInterface plus the seven FoundationXML Swift sources. Later SSH via both frp-tip.com:56267 and 10.62.230.12:2222 accepted TCP and immediately closed the session; no new Swift source failure was observed in that disconnected window.
mainline_probe_unxip_direct_binary: 2026-08-02 the efficient FoundationXML route completed by manually building _CFXMLInterface plus the seven FoundationXML Swift sources from the XML-enabled probe graph while reusing validated Foundation artifacts. foundationxml-irhandoff-20260802-214017.log and relink-foundationxml-probe2-20260802-214626.log ended LINK_RC=0 and SIGN_RC=0. verify-foundationxml-import-ninjadispatch-20260802-215708.log returned TYPECHECK_RC=0 using the generated libdispatch module.modulemap through VFS overlay. verify-foundationxml-import-only-exe-20260802-220216.log and verify-foundationxml-xmldoc-exe-20260802-220452.log compiled, signed, and ran with RUN_RC=0; the XMLDocument smoke printed toc. The xz/5.6.2 Conan cache at /storage/Users/currentUser/.conan2/p/xz22c09c364bc26/p supplies include/lzma.h and lib/liblzma.a, and probe-lzma-import-with-xz-cache-env-20260802-221415.log returned TYPECHECK_RC=0. Full direct unxip typecheck passed in typecheck-unxip-direct-parseaslib-20260802-222300.log. SwiftPM unxip release remains blocked at a process orchestration boundary: unxip-spm-release-irhandoff-j2-20260802-223538-b64.log shows swift-build sleeping in do_rt_sigsuspend with no frontend children/log growth and the probe was stopped as BUILD_STOPPED_BY_CODEX. Direct Swift 6 optimized unxip build through the proven OHOS IR handoff passed in unxip-direct-swiftc-irhandoff-concurrencyfix2-20260802-225605.log with emit-ir rc=0 size=3656085, opt rc=0, clang rc=0 object-size=903152, BUILD_RC=0, SIGN_RC=0, and HELP_RUN_RC=0. Output binary /storage/Users/currentUser/swift-mainline-ohos-src/tmp/unxip-direct-irhandoff-20260802-225607 uses OHOS musl loader, RUNPATH to staged Swift/Foundation/Dispatch/libxml2/xz paths, and expected NEEDED Swift runtimes plus libFoundationXML.so, libFoundation.so, libswiftDispatch.so, libdispatch.so, libz.so, libxml2.so.16, and libc.so. Temporary source fixes proven on device are symlink materialization, include_next shim headers, package/dependency include paths passed to ClangImporter, parse-as-library, and two actor-local continuation calls patched with isolation self. Remaining reviewable work is SwiftPM unxip process integration and formalizing IR handoff/modulewrap/runtime staging/signing/SDK propagation.
mainline_probe_unxip_swiftpm_success: 2026-08-02 a longer monitored SwiftPM release unxip run showed the earlier swift-build pause was not a permanent hang. unxip-spm-release-irhandoff-longmon-j1-t1-20260802-234731.log completed Build complete in 211.85s. The libunxip IR handoff emitted non-empty IR despite frontend rc=133, opt returned rc=0, and OHOS clang objectization produced a 699192-byte object. The normal SwiftPM release executable at /storage/Users/currentUser/swift-mainline-ohos-src/tmp/unxip-3.3-src/.build/aarch64-unknown-linux-ohos/release/unxip ran unxip --help with HELP_RC=0 and audits as an OHOS musl executable with expected Swift/Foundation/Dispatch runtime dependencies. Remaining work is Conan recipe integration and formalizing IR handoff, modulewrap, SDK/resource propagation, runtime staging, signing, symlink materialization, and Swift 6 actor-isolation source fixes into reviewable toolchain/package behavior.
